Practical No: 9
Title
CRUD Application using Angular, Node.js, and MongoDB
Aim
To develop a simple CRUD application using Angular as the frontend, Node.js with
Express as the backend, and MongoDB as the database for managing student records, with
form validation and user notifications.

Software Requirements
● Node.js
● Angular CLI
● MongoDB (Local or MongoDB Atlas)
● Visual Studio Code
● Web Browser (Chrome)

Procedure
1. Create an Angular application using Angular CLI.
2. Design components for adding, viewing, editing, and deleting student records.
3. Implement form validation in Angular forms.
4. Create a Node.js backend using Express framework.
5. Define REST API endpoints for Create, Read, Update, and Delete operations.
6. Connect the backend to MongoDB using Mongoose.
7. Integrate Angular frontend with backend APIs using HTTP services.
8. Display success and error notifications to the user.
9. Deploy the frontend on Netlify and backend on Vercel/Render.

Result
The CRUD application was successfully implemented using Angular, Node.js, and
MongoDB. The application allows users to create, read, update, and delete student records
with proper validation and notifications. The application was deployed successfully and is
accessible online.
